  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Gulam Rizwan Gulam Jilani vs The State Of Maharashtra And Another on 19 June, 2024 Author: Shivkumar Dige Bench: Shivkumar Dige aba245.24 -1- In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Bench At Aurangabad 960 Anticipatory Bail Application No. 245 Of 2024 Gulam Rizwan Gulam Jilani Versus The State of Maharashtra and another ... Advocate for Applicant : Mr. Gaurav L. Deshpande App for Respondents: Mr. R.B. Dhaware ..... Coram : Shivkumar Dige, J. Dated : 19th June, 2024. Per Court :- 1.",
    "facts": "On receiving the information, the police raided at the house of Gajanan Kale and Gulam Rizwan Gulam Jilani vs The State Of Maharashtra And Another on 19 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/199870806/ 1 found the stock of Gutkha. The police has seized the Gutkha from the house of co-accused Gajanan Kale. The custodial interrogation of the applicant is not required. The said Gutkha was purchased from the applicant. Hence he requested to reject the application. (ii) In the event of arrest of the applicant in connection with FIR No. 62 of 2023 registered with Himayatnagar Police Station, District Nanded, for the offence punishable under sections 188, 272, 273, 328 of I.P.C. and sections 26(2) (i), 26(2)(iv), 27(3)(e), 30(2)(a) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, the applicant be released on executing personal bond in the sum of Rs.15,000/- with one surety of the like amount, on the following condition :- (a) the applicant shall attend the concerned police station as and when required by the Investigating Officer. (SHIVKUMAR DIGE, J.) rlj/ Gulam Rizwan Gulam Jilani vs The State Of Maharashtra And Another on 19 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/199870806/ 3",
    "arguments": "3. It is the contention of the learned counsel for the applicant that the applicant's name has been falsely implicated in the F.I.R. No Gutkha is seized from the house of the applicant."
  },
